# Domain-coloured cryo-EM density map (Maciag 2025, PNAS Fig. 1A style)
# Run in UCSF ChimeraX: File > Open this file, or paste the lines into the command line.
# Edit the marked blocks. Chain IDs and residue ranges are placeholders.

close session

# EDIT 1: EMDB ID of the map (becomes #1) and PDB ID of the fitted model (becomes #2)
open emdb:XXXXX
open pdb:XXXX
hide #2 models

# EDIT 2: contour level from the EMDB entry (recommended level)
volume #1 style surface level 0.02 color gray

# Fig. 1A look: white background, flat light, black outlines
set bgColor white
lighting flat
graphics silhouettes true width 1.5 color black
camera ortho

# EDIT 3: colour the atoms of each domain. "color zone" paints map patches in the colour of the nearest atoms.
color #2 gray
color #2/A:1-205    yellow       # prodomain
color #2/A:206-475  magenta      # metalloproteinase
color #2/A:476-575  cyan         # disintegrin
color #2/A:576-650  lime green   # cysteine-rich
color #2/A:651-700  firebrick    # transmembrane
color #2/B          tan          # partner protein (for example iRhom2)
color #2/H,L        gray         # antibody Fab

color zone #1 near #2 distance 4 sharpEdges true

# View: front, then rotate 180 degrees about the vertical axis for the second view
view
turn y 180
